a never-before-seen portrait of princess  diana is now on display at kensington  palace  and no surprise here she looks stunning  in the black and white photo the late  princess who was 27 at the time looks  away from the camera diana wears a  one-shoulder gown and diamond earrings  while sporting her signature feathered  hair the portrait which is now part of  the new exhibition life through a royal  lens was taken by renowned photographer  david bailey in 1988 at the princess of  wales home kensington palace the image  which was shot nine years before diana's  death was originally commissioned for  the national portrait gallery but bayley  decided to keep it in his personal  archives until now  and diana's photograph is reminding fans  of similar picks the ones kate middleton  took for her 40th birthday in january  photos that show the duchess of  cambridge paying tribute to her late  mother-in-law that's really what matters  to me kate looks flawless showing off  jewelry that once belonged to princess  die specifically diamond and pearl drop  earrings and a white ruffled dress by  alexander mcqueen we're seeing the  duchess in a very different light i  think there is a new confidence about  her i think that comes with age she is  now 40 she is very confident poised  self-assured woman and with a great  sense of humor a lot of talent some of  which we're only just learning about and  while kate's dedication to giving back  certainly pays homage to her late  mother-in-law the duchess is also  working hard to create a unique lane of  her own i think one of the great  successes of the duchess of cambridge is  that she hasn't tried to carry on  diana's legacy she hasn't tried to fill  those  shoes which are of course impossible to  fill what kate's done and i think what  her greatest success has been is to  carve her own role for herself within  the royal family i mean she inherits the  title the princess of wales no one has  had that title since diana um but i  think where kate has been so clever is  to  create  her own  prototype of the princess of wales  through the work that she and william do  putting the spotlight on on those who  don't have a voice she is of course  continuing diana's legacy it's important  to her it's of course hugely important  to william  but what kate's doing is putting her own  stamp onto that title which she will one  day inherit and i think now we are  seeing the seeds that have been sewn we  are seeing the work that she's put 10  years into now coming to fruition and  it's work that really is making a  difference  [Music]  [Music]
 

